				</ukm:Metadata><Primary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/body" NumberOfProvisions="24" RestrictStartDate="2026-03-15"><Pblock DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/crossheading/state-pension-credit-entitlement-and-amount" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/crossheading/state-pension-credit-entitlement-and-amount" NumberOfProvisions="5" id="crossheading-state-pension-credit-entitlement-and-amount" RestrictExtent="E+W+S" RestrictStartDate="2023-11-16"><Title>State pension credit: entitlement and amount</Title><P1group RestrictStartDate="2024-06-08" ConfersPower="true" RestrictExtent="E+W+S"><Title> Exclusions</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/4" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/4" id="section-4"><Pnumber PuncAfter=""><CommentaryRef Ref="c4497441"/><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a8"/>4</Pnumber><P1para><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/1" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/1" id="section-4-1"><Pnumber>1</Pnumber><P2para><Text>A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a  <Substitution ChangeId="key-a9" CommentaryRef="key-a9">couple</Substitution>  the other member of which is entitled to state pension credit.</Text></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/1A" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/1A" id="section-4-1A"><Pnumber><Addition ChangeId="key-a10" CommentaryRef="key-a10">1A</Addition></Pnumber><P2para><Text><Addition ChangeId="key-a10" CommentaryRef="key-a10">A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not attained the qualifying age.</Addition></Text></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/2" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/2" id="section-4-2"><Pnumber>2</Pnumber><P2para><Text>In section 115(1) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (c. 33)

					(exclusion of certain persons from benefits) in the words preceding paragraph (a), after “Jobseekers Act 1995” insert <InlineAmendment>“
                  or to state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002
                ”</InlineAmendment>.</Text></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/3" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/3" id="section-4-3"><Pnumber>3</Pnumber><P2para><Text>Where the amount payable by way of state pension credit would (apart from this subsection) be less than a prescribed amount, it shall not be payable except in prescribed circumstances.</Text></P2para></P2></P1para></P1></P1group></Pblock></Body></Primary><Commentaries><Commentary id="c4497441" Type="I"><Para><Text>S. 4 partly in force; s. 4 not in force at Royal Assent, see s. 22(3); s. 4 in force for certain purposes at 2.7.2002 by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2002/1691" id="c00023" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2002" Number="1691">S.I. 2002/1691</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c00024" CitationRef="c00023" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2002/1691/article/2" SectionRef="article-2" Operative="true">art. 2</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a9" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in s. 4(1) substituted (5.12.2005) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2004/33" id="c3tzyhwq3-00007" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct" Year="2004" Number="33" Title="Civil Partnership Act 2004">Civil Partnership Act 2004 (c. 33)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c3tzyhwq3-00008" CitationRef="c3tzyhwq3-00007" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2004/33/section/263/8/d" SectionRef="section-263-8-d">s. 263(8)(d)</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef id="c3tzyhwq3-00009" CitationRef="c3tzyhwq3-00007" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2004/33/schedule/24/paragraph/140" SectionRef="schedule-24-paragraph-140" Operative="true">Sch. 24 para. 140</CitationSubRef>; <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2005/3175" id="c3tzyhwq3-00010" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2005" Number="3175" Title="The Civil Partnership Act 2004 